": "to think only about yourself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Vanessa thinks that Marco is self-absorbed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nincompoop", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a foolish or stupid person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sometimes Marco acts like a nincompoop.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le10ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Habits of the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> express a pattern of action that occurred regularly in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Both <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would</span> are followed by the base form of a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">used to</span> + verb<br/><span class=\"italic\">I used to take a walk everyday.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + <span class=\"italic\">would</span> + verb<br/><span class=\"italic\">I would walk 3 miles every evening.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Used to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I used to binge-watch TV shows with my brother on snow days.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We would watch all the episodes back to back.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My old boyfriend used to be impulsive</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">We would watch 3 movies in one day.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I used to love playing in the snow.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I would stay outside all afternoon.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Had Better</span>  and <span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> for what is Advisable", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\"> had better</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> to give advice. You can also use <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> to express a recommendation. <br>You can use the contraction <span class=\"italic\">'d better</span> when you speak.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\"><span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> is a strong request or advice.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We ought to make a reservation soon</span> = It's very good idea to do it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\"><span class=\"italic\">Might want to</span> is a suggestion</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You might want to call Marco to put off lunch tomorrow</span> = I suggest that you call Marco.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"bullet\"><span class=\"italic\">Had better</span> can be used as a strong recommendation, or warning.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">We'd better not drive anywhere in the snowstorm.</span> = I strongly recommend that we not drive anywhere because it's dangerous.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you are thinking of staying here for another night, you ought to call your boss.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We'd better book another night in this hotel if we need to stay here longer.", "t